1. Availability SLI (Service Level Indicator)

Definition: The proportion of login API requests that succeed out of all valid login requests received over given time window.

Formula:

    Availability SLI = (Successful Login Requests (HTTP 2xx) / Total Valid Login Requests) * 100%


2. SLO (Service Level Objective)

Target: 99.9% of login API requests succeed over a rolling 30-day (monthly) window.

3. Monthly Error Budget Calculation

Error Budget Percentage: 
        100% - 99.9% = 0.1% allowed failed/unavailable requests per month

Time Equivalent
        Total minutes in 30 days:
            30*24*60 = 43200 minutes
        Allowed downtime/errorbudget in time:
            43200 * 0.001 = 3000 failed requests

4. What happens when the Error Budget is Exhausted

Release Freeze/Gating: Non-critical features deployments and risky changes are paused until reliability recovers within  the SLO window.
Engineering Priority Shift: DEvelopment and SRE efforts shifts from shipping new features to reliability work.
Systematic Improvement: Incidents are reviewed through blameless postmortems focused on process, tooling, and gaps reather than blaming individuals.
